== B. H_4 = rank one + monomial (7 gates); how far can 'monomial + low rank' go ==
H4 - u v^T = [[0, 0, 0, 2], [0, -2, 0, 0], [0, 0, -2, 0], [2, 0, 0, 0]]  non-zeros per row: [1, 1, 1, 1]
7-gate program equals H4 on the unit vectors: True
  N=  4  rank(H/sqrt(N) - tensor monomial) = 1   trace bound (N - sqrt N)/2 = 1   rank(H/sqrt(N) - I) = 2
  N= 16  rank(H/sqrt(N) - tensor monomial) = 6   trace bound (N - sqrt N)/2 = 6   rank(H/sqrt(N) - I) = 8
  N= 64  rank(H/sqrt(N) - tensor monomial) = 28   trace bound (N - sqrt N)/2 = 28   rank(H/sqrt(N) - I) = 32
== C. Schur-Weyl: the transform is nearly free in the basis that splits by total spin ==
   blocks of size d=k-2j+1 with multiplicity C(k,j)-C(k,j-1); dense cost sum(mult*d^2)/n, and the share where H is a scalar
